# Project foundations

- Build a Persian-first Z-Tech website. Default document language is Persian (`fa`) and UI direction is RTL (`dir="rtl"`). Treat RTL as a layout concern, not a final mirroring pass.
- Treat `@docs/design-system.md` as the sole branding and visual source of truth.
- Treat `@docs/apple-design-system.md` as the reference for interaction quality, motion, layout refinement, and visual polish. Apply its principles selectively; do not copy every technique into every interface.
- Treat `@docs/content-structure.md` as the approved content and information-architecture source of truth.
- Never invent company facts, testimonials, statistics, customers, case-study outcomes, certifications, or claims. Keep placeholders clearly marked until verified content is supplied.
- When sources appear to disagree, preserve approved content, follow the brand design system for visual identity, and use the Apple reference only for interaction/refinement.
- Avoid generic AI/SaaS visual patterns. Favor deliberate typography, whitespace, hierarchy, and composition over gradients, glow, decorative effects, and repetitive card grids.
- Do not rewrite source-of-truth documents unless the user explicitly requests it.

